  "solution": "**Logic : (Cube of 1st number + Cube of 3rd number) / 2 = 2nd number**\n\nGiven :\n\n \n• \n \n(3, 14, 1)\n\n \n\n⇒{(3)³ + (1)³ over 2} = 14\n\n⇒{27 + 1 over 2} = 14\n\n⇒{28 over 2} = 14\n\n⇒14 = 14 (LHS = RHS)\n\n \n• (4, 36, 2)​\n\n⇒{(4)³ + (2)³ over 2} = 36\n\n⇒{64 + 8 over 2} = 36\n\n⇒{72 over 2} = 36\n\n⇒36 = 36 (LHS = RHS)\n\nSo,\n\n \n• Option - (1) : (8, 12, 2)​\n\n⇒{(8)³ + (2)³ over 2} = 12\n\n⇒{512 + 8 over 2} = 12\n\n⇒{520 over 2} = 12\n\n⇒260 ≠ 12 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\n \n• Option - (2) : (5, 81, 4)\n\n⇒{(5)³ + (4)³ over 2} = 81\n\n⇒{125 + 64 over 2} = 81\n\n⇒{189 over 2} = 81\n\n⇒94.5 ≠ 81 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\n \n• Option - (3) : (7, 40, 3)\n\n⇒{(7)³ + (3)³ over 2} = 40\n\n⇒{343 + 27 over 2} = 40\n\n⇒{370 over 2} = 40\n\n⇒185 ≠ 40 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\n \n• Option - (4) : (8, 260, 2)\n\n⇒{(8)³ + (2)³ over 2} = 260\n\n⇒{512 + 8 over 2} = 260\n\n⇒{520 over 2} = 260\n\n**⇒260 = 260 (LHS = RHS)**\n\nHence, **\"Option - (4)\"** is the correct answer.\n\n51",
